{"id":"23439079-10d8-4c97-ac3b-f3ea5df6257b","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6c930d8112154b2c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/capabilities/findings.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7851c9a8332527abc4941995254fe1e694383945","start":3375,"end":3422},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","placed",".","get","(","uri",")","!==","known",")","{","return",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"91e903a7b7c58775#0","after":"c0b51f841b2e5443"}},"payload":{"text":"(closed meanwhile: its findings went with it)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:33.173Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:33.173Z"}
{"id":"31d56ff8-1f9a-4bc5-b4fb-2554b2a68b4a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"32ca3768ae5b00fa","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/capabilities/findings.ts","baseline":{"blob":"413b907946aa5bde12b814492eb57f878b93172e","start":0,"end":75},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","ObservedExtension","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api/runtime","\""]},"context":{"after":"f2517b5f32f25ee8"}},"payload":{"text":"The capability findings, shown: each open TypeScript/JavaScript document's (the plugin's `_capabilities.findings` —\nengine.findings over the tree the TypeScript server holds) as this extension's own diagnostics — source\n\"capabilities\", code 900100; a dangerous capability a warning, the rest a hint — so they're squiggles, in Problems\n(the warnings) and in the hover.\n\nAsked of what's in an editor: once it's shown and has settled, once its edits have, and again while the canary is still\nrunning (`pending`) or the server isn't up yet. Not of every document VS Code holds, nor the moment one opens: that's a request\nto the server per model, a few of them each retried, before the server has been told of the file. The plugin only answers:\nnothing is put into the TypeScript server's own diagnostics, so whatever hosts the readings later (TypeScript 7's API\nconnection) answers the same request.\n\nEach says how it's decided, and is as loud as that asks for (decisions.ts): a call a run would stop at, or that's denied, is\nin Problems; one that's been allowed goes quiet. Its lightbulb decides it. And what people answered at it in their runs,\nallowed once or refused (exceptions.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:48.846Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:48.846Z"}
{"id":"3f1f10c5-7835-473f-8b6e-c1ed7beec69d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"03d7a2a7b0e21169#0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/capabilities/findings.ts","baseline":{"blob":"204d67a705455fc95541be4fcbc525aea6412910","start":2069,"end":2078},"shape":{"type":"Keyword","atoms":["interface"]},"context":{"before":"103b626ac53efe3a","after":"edcf137b42d2e8b7#0"}},"payload":{"text":"What `_capabilities.findings` answers.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:38.955Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:25:38.955Z"}
